{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "73019d19-ce90-871d-b2d1-17a2f6a3078f",
  "created_at": "2025-12-03T10:03:25-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Zoning and Inspections",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Rui Pacheco",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Anita Chaudhry",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-03T09:59:52-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Zoning and Inspections, this is Anita. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-03T09:59:56-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, good morning. Um, my name is Rui Pacheco. I'm calling for my mother. She's putting in a pool at her house and I have some questions about the fence."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-03T10:00:06-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure, I can help with that. What's the address?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-03T10:00:10-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It's four... three... three. Four thirty-three Admiral Kalbfus Road. In the North End."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-03T10:00:15-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Four thirty-three Admiral Kalbfus. Got it. And is the pool already approved, or are you still in the planning stage?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-03T10:00:22-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Still planning. The pool company is going to build it, I think this spring. But she wants to get the fence sorted first. So, what are the rules for the barrier around a pool? Like, does it have to be a certain height?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-03T10:00:36-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Generally, yes. Pools need a barrier of a minimum height, with a self-closing, self-latching gate. The inspector goes over the details when the plans come in. What kind of fence are you thinking about?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-03T10:00:48-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Um, black aluminum. Five feet tall. The kind with the flat top and the straight bars."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-03T10:00:54-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, that's a pretty common choice. Spacing between the bars matters too, so the contractor will want to check that. So what's your main question, do you need a permit for it?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-03T10:01:05-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, that's the main thing. Does the fence need a permit? Or is it only the pool?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-03T10:01:11-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Both, most likely. A fence around a pool usually needs a permit on its own, separate from the pool permit. I'd plan on that."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-03T10:01:20-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. And, um, who pulls it? Does the contractor handle the permit, or does the owner have to do it?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-03T10:01:27-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Either can. A lot of contractors file it for the homeowner, but then it's good to confirm that in writing with them. If the owner files, she'd need to come in or submit the application with a site plan showing where the fence goes."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-03T10:01:42-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A site plan. Okay. [pause] And does the neighbor have to be notified? Like, if the fence is near the property line?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-03T10:01:50-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I don't believe there's a general notification requirement for a fence. But the fence has to sit on her own property, so if the line is unclear, she may want a survey. Do you know if it's close to the line?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-03T10:02:04-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I think it's about, um, three feet in from the line on the left side. I'm not sure. I'd have to check."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-03T10:02:12-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's worth measuring. If you want, I can have someone from the building side call your mother back with specifics on the setback and the barrier requirements."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-03T10:02:21-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, please. You can use my number. It's four, zero, one. Five, five, five. Zero, one, six, three."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-03T10:02:28-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Four-oh-one, five-five-five, zero-one-six-three. And that's Rui?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-03T10:02:31-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. R, U, I. Pacheco."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-03T10:02:34-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you. I'll send that over today. They're usually back to people within a day or two."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-03T10:02:40-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, good. That works. Um, one more thing. If the pool is not until spring, can we put the fence up first, or should we wait?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-03T10:02:49-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You can get the permit and build the fence first, as long as it's approved. Just make sure the gate and the height match what the pool requires, so you don't redo it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-03T10:03:00-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. That's good, because the ground is soft in spring and I want to be done before the garden. I do raised beds in the back, so I'm planning the seed orders now anyway."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-03T10:03:12-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Makes sense, get the fence work done before the planting. Anything else I can help with today?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-03T10:03:18-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, that's everything. Thank you for your time."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-03T10:03:22-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're welcome, Rui. Have a good day."
    }
  ],
